  "decisionD168Recorded": true,
  "nextAction": "Integrate and validate the staged S15 saved-journey capacity work from s15-journey-capacity. The existing 32-record bound already preserves history without eviction, but new-route actions currently give a generic rejection and a full-history migration has no capacity explanation. Expose historyCapacity and per-route canStart, show a full-only RU/EN 32/32 notice explaining deliberate deletion of one chosen history entry, disable only starts needing a new record, and provide an explicit focus-safe Go to history action. Existing-record resume, Next and selection must remain usable. Prove full-capacity same-record resume, blocked new-slot start/migration and explicit one-record deletion recovery, retaining storage readback/failure authority and never automatically clearing or evicting records. Preserve current-policy prerequisites, independent migration review, confirmation focus ownership, paused cold restoration and canonical scene ownership. Production inventories stay empty; reviewed content, child profiles, narration, formal accessibility, installed-device/performance, iOS and stage/release acceptance remain pending. S03.acceptance stays first unresolved.",
  "limitations": [
    "Eight selected actual-App Chrome cases use synthetic journey/migration providers. Three new cases cover keyboard activation, ownership-aware focus restoration when save completion invalidates deletion consent, outside focus retention, explicit cancellation and fresh-document/native-background lifecycle. Five existing journey, cold restoration, future-schema deletion, migration and history cases are rerun. These are bounded local checks, not a full keyboard, screen-reader or accessibility audit.",
    "The original 580 unit tests from 22 files are retained with their original history source manifest, raw report and execution logs; no unit rerun is claimed. All 22 unit files and 1,620 protected source inputs, including unchanged runtime dependencies, retain exact hashes. The four changed UI controls are validated by fresh TypeScript and browser checks. Prior 13-case history proof and its inspected captures remain separately linked to their original source.",
    "Focus restoration follows the user's current focus ownership. An invalidated owned confirmation returns focus to stable status or heading; a user-selected outside control retains focus. Confirmation is transient and fenced by current revisions. Keyboard cancellation restores its own trigger. Persisted semantic progress remains unchanged by cancellation, document restoration and native background; no consent replay or automatic movement is added.",
    "Production journey and migration inventories remain empty and all 34 existing RU/EN dialogue records remain draft. Synthetic receipts confer no editorial approval. Exact-version current-policy prerequisites, independently reviewed explicit migration, preservation of original history, unsupported-save protection and truthful storage failure/retry retain their prior boundaries. Semantic acknowledgements are not books-read claims.",
    "Fresh preserved PWA and Android-dev artifacts bind the exact source. Built-PWA coverage is the existing offline/download smoke; local APK bytes, manifests and signatures do not establish installed-device execution. The controlled native-preference fixture tests the App/adapter contract, not physical-device durability. No iOS build, child access, narration, entitlement, deployment, store submission or release is performed."
  ],
